  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Given name then family name, Western style. Pākehā (New Zealanders of European descent) mostly have English, Scottish and Irish names. Many Māori carry an English first name alongside or instead of a Māori one, and family names that are Māori (Ngata, Hēnare, Tipene, Parata) or English (Walker, Brown); Māori names are written with macrons on long vowels. Samoan and Tongan families often have biblical first names in Pacific form (Sione for John, Tavita or Tevita for David, Mele for Mary), and chiefly titles can become surnames (Tuilagi, Fuimaono). Auckland also has large Chinese, Indian, Korean and Filipino communities.",
